{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "_readme": [
    "Asset registry for the dedicated modality tests: tests/test_text.py,",
    "tests/test_images.py and tests/test_videos.py.",
    "",
    "This file holds the assets those tests add on top of what already lives in",
    "the repo (tests/detector_assets.json, tests/calibration_corpus/, 'test videos/').",
    "It is kept separate from tests/detector_assets.json so adding assets here",
    "does not silently widen the scope of scripts/regression_check.py (which",
    "scans that file).",
    "",
    "Schema per entry:",
    "  id        stable test id (printed in every run)",
    "  label     'ai' | 'human'   ground truth the verdict is checked against",
    "  kind      'video' (social post resolved with yt-dlp, or a direct media URL)",
    "  source    free-text provenance of the asset",
    "  url       the post/page URL",
    "  note      what the clip is, as reported by the user who supplied it",
    "",
    "'label' is the expected class for the PASS/FAIL column. Every entry was",
    "supplied as an AI-generated clip, except ig-DecK8wQPTM7: the user was unsure",
    "about that one and later confirmed it IS authentic (Instagram labels it AI,",
    "the detector reads it authentic too), so it is labeled 'human' and its note",
    "records the confirmation."
  ],
